<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa '97 maize, sunseed estimates sharply down.</title>
<headline>S.Africa '97 maize, sunseed estimates sharply down.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Crop Estimates Committee said on Thursday it estimated the 1997 maize crop at 7.564 million tonnes, sharply down from last year's 9.484 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This year's crop was expected to comprise 4.002 million tonnes of white maize and 3.562 million tonnes of yellow, the committee said in its first official estimate for the new season.</p>
<p>Last year's maize crop comprised 5.440 million tonnes of white maize and 4.044 million tonnes of yellow.</p>
<p>The first official sunflower seed estimate for 1997 forecast a crop of 450,000 tonnes also well down on last year's 730,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
